 "poem": "183, The Commencement of the Composition of\nI. Adieu! Some Maidens have disappeared,\nLike stars whose brightness shall not return; you\nOf modest beauty there are only\nSome who for your sake have left their away,\nAnd some who with less longing desire you,\nBut all whom I see on hill and Meadow.\n204, Poem on the Last Year's Courtly Holiday\nThe solid heart which year after year\nMay carry on in his youth's desire;\nThe goodliest hands that never wearied him\nBy any one gift he could receive.",
